        "x1": 72.2,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "100"
      },
      {
        "y": 23.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 261.5,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "In the headlines"
      },
      {
        "y": 70.5,
        "x0": 75.1,
        "x1": 264.9,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "A Features of headline language"
      },
      {
        "y": 88,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 425.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "If a story hits the headlines it suddenly receives a lot of attention in the news."
      },
      {
        "y": 100,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 519,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Here are two typical examples of headlines from tabloid newspapers with comments on their use of"
      },
      {
        "y": 112.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 364.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "language. [popular papers with small pages and short simple reports]"
      },
      {
        "y": 130.7,
        "x0": 108.8,
        "x1": 356.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "EXPERT REVEALS NEW CLOUD DANGERS"
      },
      {
        "y": 152.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 422,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "• Articles, prepositions and auxiliary verbs are often omitted from headlines."
      },
      {
        "y": 164.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 510.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "• This use of the present simple instead of the past tense makes the story sound more immediate."
      },
      {
        "y": 176.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 511.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "• The use of language is often ambiguous. It is not entirely clear, for example, what cloud refers to"
      },
      {
        "y": 188.9,
        "x0": 110.6,
        "x1": 513.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "here. It is actually about the dangers of storing electronic information on a ‘cloud’ [hosted services"
      },
      {
        "y": 200.9,
        "x0": 110.6,
        "x1": 520.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "on the internet for storing personal data], but it could have referred to dangers relating to the weather."
      },
      {
        "y": 212.9,
        "x0": 110.6,
        "x1": 331.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Readers have to look at the story in order to find out."
      },
      {
        "y": 224.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 381.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "• Words with dramatic associations such as danger are often used."
      },
      {
        "y": 242.7,
        "x0": 112.9,
        "x1": 352.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "TV STAR TRAGIC TARGET FOR CRAZED GUNMAN"
      },
      {
        "y": 265.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 481.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "This story is about how a well-known television actor was shot by a mentally unstable killer."
      },
      {
        "y": 277.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 507.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "• In order to attract readers’ attention, tabloid newspapers often feature celebrities, e.g. film/pop"
      },
      {
        "y": 289.9,
        "x0": 110.6,
        "x1": 235.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "stars and sports personalities."
      },
      {
        "y": 301.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 514.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "• Alliteration such as TV Star Tragic Target is often used to attract the eye in headlines and to make"
      },
      {
        "y": 313.9,
        "x0": 110.6,
        "x1": 238.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "them sound more memorable."
      },
      {
        "y": 325.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 498.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "• Newspapers tend to use strong, simple words such as ‘gunman’ in order to express an idea or"
      },
      {
        "y": 337.9,
        "x0": 110.6,
        "x1": 286.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "image as briefly and as vividly as possible."
      },
      {
        "y": 349.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 495.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "• Strongly emotional words like crazed are often used to attract attention. [behaving in a wild or"
      },
      {
        "y": 362.8,
        "x0": 110.6,
        "x1": 301.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "strange way, especially because of strong emotion]"
      },
      {
        "y": 382.8,
        "x0": 74.7,
        "x1": 175.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "B Violent words"
      },
      {
        "y": 400.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 514.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Violent and militaristic words are often used in headlines, especially in tabloid newspapers, in order"
      },
      {
        "y": 412.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 511.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "to make stories seem more dramatic. For example, people who cause trouble may be referred to as"
      },
      {
        "y": 424.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 187.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "thugs, yobs or louts."
      },
      {
        "y": 444.9,
        "x0": 113,
        "x1": 403.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "EU acts to crush1 terror of thugs Crackdown2 on soccer louts"
      },
      {
        "y": 472,
        "x0": 160,
        "x1": 289.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Palace besieged3 by journalists"
      },
      {
        "y": 476.7,
        "x0": 340.3,
        "x1": 434.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Language help"
      },
      {
        "y": 496.8,
        "x0": 109.7,
        "x1": 227.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Typhoon rips4 through town"
      },
      {
        "y": 501,
        "x0": 341.3,
        "x1": 497.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "The kind of language that is common in"
      },
      {
        "y": 513,
        "x0": 341.3,
        "x1": 489.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "headlines may sound strange in other"
      },
      {
        "y": 521.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 132,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "1 destroy"
      },
      {
        "y": 525,
        "x0": 341.3,
        "x1": 502.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "contexts. So the vocabulary in this unit is"
      },
      {
        "y": 532.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 281.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "2 taking serious measures to deal with a problem"
      },
      {
        "y": 537,
        "x0": 341.3,
        "x1": 500.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "more likely to be useful to you when you"
      },
      {
        "y": 543.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 199.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "3 surrounded, as if by army"
      },
      {
        "y": 549,
        "x0": 341.3,
        "x1": 487.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "are reading rather than when you are"
      },
      {
        "y": 554.7,
